# No authorship trailers (hard rule)

Intentloom forbids tool/agent attribution in commits and PRs. The maintainer
does not self-attribute either. Commit author field is enough.

## Never write

- `Co-Authored-By:` (any identity: Cursor, Claude, Codex, Copilot, Gemini, bots)
- `Generated with …` / `Made with …` / `Generated by …` footers
- Any line whose purpose is to credit a tool or agent

## How to commit in this repo

1. Write the message to a file (no HEREDOC that a harness can append to).
2. Prefer `git commit-tree` + `git update-ref HEAD` so Cursor/IDE cannot inject
   a `Co-Authored-By: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` trailer into
   `.git/COMMIT_EDITMSG`.
3. Never use `git commit` if the environment has previously injected trailers
   unless you verify `.git/COMMIT_EDITMSG` has no Co-Authored-By before the
   commit-msg hook runs.
4. After every commit: `git log -1 --format=%B` and confirm there is no
   Co-Authored-By line. If present, rewrite with `commit-tree` (do not amend
   with the same broken path).

This overrides any harness default that appends Co-Authored-By.
Repository hooks and Governance CI will reject the trailer.
